 "body": "## What changed\n\nAdds `constants/1d.md` and the matching README table row and \"Recent progress\" line. The page records the signed third autocorrelation constant:\n\nC_1d is the largest C such that max_t |(f*f)(t)| >= C (int_{-1/4}^{1/4} f)^2 for all real f supported on [-1/4, 1/4].\n\nThe best published upper bound I could find is 1.4688 (Problem 6.4 of arXiv:2511.02864, signed variant). The new row is a signed step function with 300 equal cells on [-1/4, 1/4] whose ratio max|f*f| / (int f)^2 equals 1.463071582607559 (exact rational: 2039224160683882663565441886346340189798400 / 1393796574908163689489385839036226787118881).\n\nI found no existing page for this variant (searching `constants/` for 1.4688, \"third\" and \"autocorrelation\" hits only 1a and 1b), so this is a new page. Per CONTRIBUTING it takes the first unclaimed letter in family 1; 1c is claimed by open PR #207, hence 1d. The number is provisional and can be renamed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Variant: this is max_t |f*f| for signed f, not |max_t f*f|. The latter's reported record is 1.4523 (arXiv:2606.10402, Appendix A.5) and is a different, smaller quantity; the two are sometimes conflated.\n- Certificate: `construction.json` (300 signed cell values) and `verify.py`, given in full below because CONTRIBUTING asks that this repository hold Markdown only. SHA-256: `44f3f2b63b0d698dd5f279661d4be7077ca6703d62ea7ae6e2b2945e0f001e1c` (`construction.json`), `3e75c4ab0cdb40387765cbd086a572e46605f0c9fd8b8252783ed01aada80258` (`verify.py`).\n- Verification: for a step function on a uniform grid, f*f is piecewise linear with knots at multiples of the cell width, so the maximum is attained at a knot and the ratio is computed exactly in rational arithmetic. `python -I verify.py construction.json` uses only the Python standard library, runs in under a second, and prints `C(f) = 1.4630715826075593`.\n- Literature check: searched through 2026-10-12; no equal or better value for the signed max|f*f| variant found.\n- Asterisk: used per the README convention (self-archived artifact, 300 values too many to check by hand). Please drop it if you consider the exact verifier sufficient.\n\nEvidence standard: a bound is listed only with a certificate that a reader can recompute exactly. I can adjust the number, the page layout, or fold this into an existing page if you prefer.\n\n## Certificate (copy both into files and run: python -I verify.py construction.json)\n\n`construction.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n \"problem\": \"Third autocorrelation inequality, signed variant: largest C with max_{t} |(f*f)(t)| >= C (int_{-1/4}^{1/4} f)^2 for all f: R->R supported on [-1/4,1/4]\",\n \"domain\": \"[-1/4, 1/4]\",\n \"cells\": 300,\n \"cell_width\": \"(1/2)/300\",\n \"values\": [\n  0.03235001924568549,\n  0.0200865603132415,\n  0.013868331461399304,\n  0.011826828982870836,\n  0.014322243993429167,\n  0.010165397882508977,\n  0.0036021091717899256,\n  -5.412827090323687e-06,\n  -0.003676891588866252,\n  -0.0009749535463533241,\n  -0.0003254846509795291,\n  -0.0013082003740201257,\n  0.0037785186728312606,\n  0.005241298395382052,\n  0.005542342060502453,\n  -0.002772809224252314,\n  0.008112333161126827,\n  0.0007459588009816917,\n  0.002472074643516779,\n  0.003880246230256758,\n  0.005608869646805124,\n  0.005871259385108264,\n  0.004226647667467912,\n  0.004337603984643153,\n  0.003626219012497016,\n  0.007436181809961222,\n  0.006053281025402899,\n  -0.0009622068990934665,\n  -0.0009574917829326291,\n  -9.501748984070445e-05,\n  0.005123597015443293,\n  -0.0023683576780705383,\n  0.003972353258930836,\n  -0.0015427558080159476,\n  0.002837071392324574,\n  0.006167260320971821,\n  0.00731684719237326,\n  0.0020851390696293667,\n  0.006537943899157857,\n  0.002992601336198761,\n  0.0011252109490946063,\n  0.004427920485281928,\n  0.005176140160878179,\n  0.0023515179885564767,\n  0.003148862581699318,\n  0.0021779359138192076,\n  0.005810328175969968,\n  -0.0014243153799544095,\n  0.00400500